{
  "original_id": "win-00077-p01",
  "archive_id": "BW2-B77-P01",
  "title": "An Every-Order Bipyramid Disproof for S₂,₁,₁ ⊔ K₂ in Maximal Planar Graphs",
  "batch_label": "77",
  "kind": "resolution-paper",
  "original_status": "disproved",
  "scope": "Let H be the seven-vertex graph S_{2,1,1} disjoint-union K_2, with copies interpreted injectively and non-induced as in problem.md. For every integer m >= 3, the bipyramid B_m = overline(K_2) + C_m is a finite simple maximal planar graph, and the edge-colouring in which every apex--rim edge is red and every rim-cycle edge is blue contains neither a red nor a blue copy of H. Since |V(B_m)| = m+2, an avoiding maximal-planar graph exists at every order n >= 5. Consequently no eventual-unavoidability threshold N exists, and the frozen assertion in source.md is false.",
  "gate_basis": "Current released terminal, manifest, PDF, TeX freeze, snapshot files, provenance and four audits agree.",
